# Pairs with BackupSagaConsistent, and answers the #4619 residual: a decision
# row pruned while a bucket of its saga is still pending. Pruning before every
# shard applied its terminal leaves the pending bucket with no local decision,
# so the capture reads it pre-saga next to a shard already post-saga. In
# production the saga calls ForgetAsync only after its broadcast acked, which
# is the precondition this mutation drops. DEADLOCK is off because the
# pruned row also strands the pending bucket for good: no sweep or
# broadcast can terminate it, so the saga never quiesces.
MODULE: BackupSagaConsistentPruneBeforeTerminals
TARGET: BackupSagaConsistent
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: an expired decision row is pruned while a bucket of its saga is still pending
PERTURBS: Prune
DEADLOCK: off

--- FIND
    /\ \A sh \in Writes("s") : term["s"][sh] # "none"
    /\ loc' = [loc EXCEPT !["s"]["T1"] = "none"]
--- REPLACE
    \* MUTATION: pruned before every terminal was applied.
    /\ loc' = [loc EXCEPT !["s"]["T1"] = "none"]
--- END